0..78 Comment "// The write that reads no holder count, kept from a string that may have been"
79..159 Comment "// copied: a grade-one hold takes only a string made where it stands, so a copy,"
160..239 Comment "// whose buffer the original holds too, is refused before any write reaches it."
241..321 Comment "// The lists; the byte lists; the owned bytes; where they live; the long string,"
322..393 Comment "// its copy and the write that counts holders; the write that does not."
